  "notes": "すねる describes a softer, more withdrawn form of sulking compared to ⟦ふてくされる→ふてくされる：09363_futekusareru⟧. While ⟦ふてくされる→ふてくされる：09363_futekusareru⟧ implies defiance and bad temper, すねる suggests feeling hurt, neglected, or left out.\n\nTypically used for:\n- Children who didn't get what they wanted\n- People feeling overlooked or ignored\n- Someone acting hurt to get attention\n\nThe behavior is often seen as somewhat childish or attention-seeking.",
